playerctl_systray
-----------------

simple and minimal system tray applet for controlling media players via playerctl.
uses AppIndicator3 for broad panel compatibility across linux desktops.

![screenshot](https://kj-media.online/pics/playerctl-systray/playerctl_systray.png)

arch linux deps (system packages)
  - python
  - python-gobject
  - libappindicator-gtk3
  - playerctl

other distros:
  - install equivalent python3, pygobject, appindicator3, and playerctl packages.

quick run
  ./playerctl_systray
  ./playerctl_systray --help
  ./playerctl_systray --version

install
  make install

  # or manually
  mkdir -p ~/.local/bin
  install -Dm755 playerctl_systray ~/.local/bin/playerctl_systray

remove
  make remove

how it works
  creates a systray icon with a dropdown menu listing active playerctl instances.
  each instance has play-pause, next, and previous controls.
  an "-a" submenu controls all players at once.
  polls every ~1s for player changes and refreshes the menu automatically.

